OL,3,GNEWSATitanic hero's postcard to sister 
OL,4,Asells for #32k                         
OL,6,FA postcard written by the Titanic's    
OL,7,Fsenior wireless operator has sold for  
OL,8,F#32,000 at auction, well over the      
OL,9,Fexpected price of up to #20,000.       
OL,11,FJack Phillips, 25, who came from       
OL,12,FSurrey, wrote the card to his sister   
OL,13,FElsie who lived in Godalming, while the
OL,14,Fship was docked in Southampton on 6    
OL,15,FApril 1912.                            
OL,17,FPhillips, who died in the disaster     
OL,18,Falongside about 1,500 others, remained 
OL,19,Fat his post sending wireless distress  
OL,20,Fcalls after the TItanic had struck an  
OL,21,Ficeberg.                               
OL,23,APub: 22-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
